arch box and look  for the first guide itgb  1.1 drag and drop to colored  cells by the guide expression levels  let's go for red  yep this cell cluster is now  highlighted these cells express the  first guide itgb 1.1  let's add the second guide annotated  counts  search for the second guide itg b  1.2 i will just use a different color  let's color them blue here we go a  different  cell cluster comes up these blue cells  expressing itgb 1.2  okay now i'm going  to focus on crisper positive cells only  with the help of our flexible selection  tool  here it is lasso tool i will just circle  around them  as you see the tool is very very  flexible  yep the legend is now red  to blue gradient cells expressing one  guide  are in red the other guide in blue and  we also see  two cells these gray dots in the middle  which express both guides at the same  time  depending on your goal you may want to  remove them  using a combination of selection  and filter tools  at this point we know which cells  express our crispr guide which is nice  but what we really want to know is  whether our targeting works to rephrase  we need to confirm the down expression  of the targeted gene  which brings me to the side c cassay and  the third layer  of omics information if crispr worked  we should see no gene expression  therefore let's examine the expression  of  itgb1 mrna  annotate it counts itgb  here it is itgb1 add as color  i will use the third color right now the  legend  is now a triangle our crisper guides are  in blue  in red as they used to be and the  expression levels of  itgb1 mrna are in green  currently selected cells are crispr  positive  and we see that crispr positive cells do  not express  itgb1 mrna let's invert the selection  and as expected crispr negative cells  do express itgb1 mrna  for the final confirmation and the  fourth layer of omics  let's see the the protein level  annotated counts the protein is cd29  green is fine i'll stick with green  and here we go negative cells  do express cd29 protein and i will  invert back crispr negative cells  do not express cd or crispr  positive cells do not express cd29  to quickly recap cell hashing crispr  gene and protein expression all on the  same cells  let's do some closing remarks  with the help of the slidac  there is a functionality that we will  release soon the search portal  it allows you to perform searches of  either your own project database  or data from public repositories  therefore you you may have restricted  access to the lab due to the current  public health situation  but you can for instance use public data  to generate or test hypotheses  we have three trials of all our packages  and to apply for your  free trial of partak flow please  use the link on the screen finally an  announcement we regularly focus  on different aspects on of  our software and host public webinars  the next  next one is going to be on trajectory  analysis  imported flow the registration is now  open you see the registration link we  would be very happy to welcome you again  thank you so much for your attention  today thank you
 

